ct it's hard to make a demo gorgon  stretch the wall given the time  constraints however the production  designer did spend a lot of time hunting  down authentic props online from eBay  they found things like Trapper Keepers  and toys from the eighties that gave the  show the same feel as those classic  films from the time period justice for  barb if fans had it their way  barb would have met with a different  fate on the show even the creators were  pretty bummed when they had to sacrifice  barb to move the story along typically  in horror movies the rebellious  teenagers who are engaging in  questionable acts are the first to go  but while Nancy was upstairs making even  more bad decisions our innocent barb was  being snagged by the demo Corrigan it  goes against everything the audience was  expecting which is the good girls and  guys are spared and the bad kids are  sacrificed to the monsters the Defra  brothers admitted that the creative team  would often shake their heads and  remorse saying poor barb fans agreed and  even started a campaign with a hashtag  justice for barb fans like Franz  Buffington posted that he went for a  late night pool swim but it didn't feel  right he wrote it was still too soon and  that he can't believe we lost her so  abruptly followed by the hashtag hashtag  justice for barb we feel you Brent's  barb was like the best friend we all  wish we had in high school the original  demo gorgon the mythology of the  gorgon goes back centuries but in the  show the kids first mentioned the demo  Gorgon during a game of Dungeons and  Dragons  while the creature goes back hundreds of  years the D&amp;D version of the demonic  beam is an 18-foot tall monster with a  scaly reptile body tentacles forearms  and two huge baboon heads it was called  the prince of demons and even in the  game it was the stuff of nightmares  but the creators of the show deviated  from the D&amp;D version of this monster  instead of two giant baboon heads they  went with